--- Delivery guarantee of a network message
declare enum Reliability
    --- Send the message unreliably, the message may be lost (with no retransmission) or received in a different order than it was sent, but is cheaper and faster to use than reliable. Use it for sending events that are transient and non critical for gameplay
    Unreliable
    --- Send the message reliably, this is guaranteed to be sent and received in order, but is more expensive to use than unreliable. Use it when you want to make sure the event is received by the other side
    Reliable
end

--- Cloud and sky rendering presets
declare enum SkyMode
    --- Uses a 3D Volumetric Cloud layer
    VolumetricClouds
    --- Designed to mimic the look of the volumetric clouds but as a static cloud texture. Much lower performance cost than volumetric clouds.
    StaticClouds
    --- Uses simple 2D dynamic clouds
    DynamicClouds2D
    --- Disables all forms of dynamic clouds
    NoClouds
    --- Trades clouds for a full 3D volumetric aurora, much more convincing than the 2D effect.
    VolumetricAurora
    --- Turns off all sky color, atmospheric scattering, clouds, etc. Specifically for environments which are set in outer space with no planet/ground beneath the camera.
    Space
end

